  "rules": [
    {
      "body": "Applies to a progress watcher whose startup can synchronously emit multiple packets and whose visible-progress callback can synchronously replace or hide its visit. For each packet, decide admission against the originating visit and attempt before decoding or recording it. If synchronous handling of an earlier packet retires that owner, reject later startup packets even while listener removal is awaiting the returned cleanup handle. Preserve exactly-once audit settlement for packets admitted before retirement, but never let their settlement repaint a retired owner; retain current-owner rendering, retry, queue records, cancellation, and ordinary later streaming. Verify reentrant selection and hiding during multi-packet startup, including delayed decode of an admitted packet and rejection of a later packet from the retired owner.",
      "category": "event_relation",
      "id": "R01"
    }
  ],
